WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.401 --> 00:00:15.673
Although they were doing nothing wrong, Laurie and Jo felt like two very naughty children.

2
00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:21.450
Sitting up straight, hands folded in their laps, neither young one dared to utter a sound.

3
00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:27.821
"You say you are too ill to have your lessons with Mr. Brookes," Mr. Laurence began.

4
00:00:27.822 --> 00:00:32.301
"My tutor," Laurie whispered under his breath to Jo.

5
00:00:32.302 --> 00:00:38.448
"Did you say something, boy?" Mr. Laurence stood menacingly in front of Laurie.

6
00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:47.465
"No, sir," squeaked Laurie, "I mean, I was telling Jo, who's our neighbor . . . you know that lovely family with all those girls,

7
00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:54.975
and Jo, here, being the second eldest . . . well, I was telling her who Brookes was, I mean, Mr. Brookes, sir."

8
00:00:54.976 --> 00:01:00.797
Jo felt a giggle in her throat as poor Laurie rambled on.

9
00:01:00.798 --> 00:01:06.281
"What's so funny, girl?" Mr. Laurence moved over to where Jo sat.

10
00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:10.504
At that moment, the whole situation seemed oddly hilarious.

11
00:01:10.505 --> 00:01:15.364
Holding back the laughter that bubbled inside was causing Jo physical pain.

12
00:01:15.365 --> 00:01:25.700
She could no longer do it. "Oh, I'm dreadfully sorry, sir," roared Jo, wiping the tears from her eyes.

13
00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:30.378
Both Laurie and his grandfather were shocked at her outburst.

14
00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:38.407
"Well, Laurie looks horribly sick and that ugly doll he's holding . . . " Jo's voice cracked but she continued,

15
00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:42.971
"As for me, I should be ladylike and not laugh out loud.

16
00:01:42.972 --> 00:01:48.227
And you . . . " Jo stopped herself before she did further damage.

17
00:01:48.228 --> 00:01:53.995
But to her astonishment, the old man looked at her with a twinkle in his eye and said,

18
00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:59.460
"Please continue. I'd like to know what is so funny about me."

19
00:01:59.461 --> 00:02:05.039
Ignoring Laurie's kicks from under the table, Jo cleared her throat and went on:

20
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:13.615
"Well, you're like a schoolmaster who has just caught his two most naughty pupils doing something terrible but he doesn't know what.

21
00:02:13.616 --> 00:02:19.856
So you're frowning and grunting and trying so hard to look upset but . . . but . . . ,"

22
00:02:19.857 --> 00:02:26.196
Jo gasped for breath, "to me, sir, it's absolutely comical."

23
00:02:26.197 --> 00:02:32.018
Still chuckling, Jo stood up and gathered her things.

24
00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:36.086
"But I understand that I was completely out of line.

25
00:02:36.087 --> 00:02:41.107
My sisters tell me that I am so boorish, that's what the youngest, Amy, says,

26
00:02:41.108 --> 00:02:47.346
and I'm sure the others agree, though Beth, being so sweet and gentle, would never tell me that to my face,

27
00:02:47.347 --> 00:02:51.021
but I do cause so much embarrassment to our family.

28
00:02:51.022 --> 00:02:56.281
So before I do any more damage, I had better leave," Jo babbled.

29
00:02:56.282 --> 00:03:01.230
She caught a glimpse of Laurie bowing his head lower and his shoulders quivering.

30
00:03:01.231 --> 00:03:05.189
"That boy is laughing at me," she said to herself.

31
00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:12.515
Resisting the temptation to give Laurie a playful punch, Jo, instead, took a deep breath, faced the old man and said,

32
00:03:12.516 --> 00:03:16.125
"Sir, may I speak freely one last time?"

33
00:03:16.126 --> 00:03:19.267
"You've been saying whatever you like until now.

34
00:03:19.268 --> 00:03:23.206
Why stop?" Mr. Laurence said in a teasing voice.

35
00:03:23.207 --> 00:03:28.009
"Well, in my opinion, sir, I think Laurie is a splendid boy.

36
00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:35.462
And what he really needs to feel better is some warm love and lots and lots of laughter," said Dr. Jo.

37
00:03:35.463 --> 00:03:42.566
Mr. Laurence was a shrewd man. He had already noticed how different Laurie seemed when he was with Jo.

38
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:46.499
The change in his grandson was a pleasant one.

39
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:52.552
"Then maybe you'd better stay and make sure he gets well," was the old man's surprising remark.

40
00:03:52.553 --> 00:03:56.845
He smiled warmly at Jo and then at his grandson.

41
00:03:56.846 --> 00:04:02.351
Later on she described Mr. Laurence's transformation to her sisters this way:

42
00:04:02.352 --> 00:04:08.904
"It was as if another person took over his body and he suddenly turned into the kindest man in the world."

43
00:04:08.905 --> 00:04:13.265
From that moment on, Laurie became the daily visitor to the March home.

44
00:04:13.266 --> 00:04:21.961
During the day he had his lessons with Mr. Brookes, a handsome intelligent young man employed by Mr. Laurence to help with his grandson's studies.

45
00:04:21.962 --> 00:04:25.754
Left with no choice after Laurie refused to attend boarding school,

46
00:04:25.755 --> 00:04:32.516
his grandfather finally agreed to let him receive home-schooling until he went off to university the following year.

47
00:04:32.517 --> 00:04:36.324
Even during his lessons, Laurie had one eye on the time.

48
00:04:36.325 --> 00:04:40.838
As the hands of the antique grandfather clock in the library inched toward four,

49
00:04:40.839 --> 00:04:50.064
Laurie's ears strained for the now-familiar sounds of his neighbors returning from their day's activities. Amy would come home first.

50
00:04:50.065 --> 00:04:56.143
Laurie recognized how she slammed the door in her impatience to shut out any memory of the school day.

51
00:04:56.144 --> 00:05:03.375
Then she would call out in a childish shrill, "Hannah! Can I have a snack? I'm so famished!"

52
00:05:03.376 --> 00:05:08.933
Meg and Jo came home around the same time but their entrance was completely different.

53
00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:16.135
Laurie never knew when Meg returned home exactly because he would not hear her going into the house like Amy.

54
00:05:16.136 --> 00:05:24.996
But from where he sat, he could see Meg walk into the kitchen, say hello to Hannah, put on her apron, and help the housekeeper prepare dinner.

55
00:05:24.997 --> 00:05:29.070
Thinking about his friend Jo brought a smile to Laurie's lips.

56
00:05:29.071 --> 00:05:36.864
Jo, knowing that Laurie would be watching out for her return, would make all kinds of noises to let him know she was home.

57
00:05:36.865 --> 00:05:41.589
One time, she started to hum a funny song as she walked up the path to their door.

58
00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:49.565
Laurie had burst out into laughter, alarming and troubling Mr. Brookes, who was in the middle of explaining a rather dismal subject.

59
00:05:49.566 --> 00:05:59.083
Then, on another occasion, Mr. Brookes was explaining a tricky mathematical problem on the blackboard when he was interrupted by a strange barking noise.

60
00:05:59.084 --> 00:06:03.440
Looking out the window, Mr. Brookes could not see any canine in the area,

61
00:06:03.441 --> 00:06:09.477
but he did happen to catch a glimpse of a girl hastily shutting the entrance door over at the March home.

62
00:06:09.478 --> 00:06:17.905
Of the four girls, Beth stayed home all day but Laurie could not make out any sounds that alerted him to where she was.

63
00:06:17.906 --> 00:06:27.489
Once, he thought he heard very soft singing, but Laurie could not be sure if it was Beth, who he knew loved to sing, or if he had imagined it.

64
00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:32.865
"As your attention has already left the lesson and moved on to the affairs in the other house,"

65
00:06:32.866 --> 00:06:37.439
Mr. Brookes declared, closing his book, "you may be excused now."

66
00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.325
Giving him a mock salute, Laurie sprang up, and leaped out of the library.

67
00:06:42.326 --> 00:06:45.538
Nothing was ever boring at the Marches' home.

68
00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:51.299
The girls always had plenty to keep themselves occupied and there was never a shortage of things to talk about.

69
00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:57.012
On this particular evening, the conversation ranged from spiders to dinner invitations.

70
00:06:57.013 --> 00:07:01.497
"Grandfather would love for all of you to come for dinner tomorrow," Laurie said.

71
00:07:01.498 --> 00:07:05.576
Although Mr. Laurence had extended the invitation on several occasions,

72
00:07:05.577 --> 00:07:12.119
Mother was delaying accepting it until Beth felt comfortable enough around Laurie to venture over to the unfamiliar house.

73
00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:16.240
"That's very kind of him," Beth replied in her soft way.

74
00:07:16.241 --> 00:07:19.885
Laurie and Jo stopped playing cards to stare at her.

75
00:07:19.886 --> 00:07:23.433
"Does that mean you'd like to come to my house?" asked Laurie.

76
00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:34.669
Beth smiled shyly at Laurie and said: "To me, you're more than a neighbor, Laurie, you're our dear friend."
